      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Our vision",
        "heading": "A more mobile India",
        "lead": "Physiotherapy should not be a last resort in a metro clinic. It should be everyday care that clinics, caregivers, and households across India can actually get.",
        "text": "<p>Nearly one in six people in India lives with musculoskeletal pain. Community studies put that close to 200 million people — and the burden is heavier in rural districts than in cities. Among Indians over 45, more than half report joint or back pain. Osteoarthritis alone touches tens of millions of knees and spines.</p><p>Pain keeps farmers from fields, nurses from shifts, and older parents from walking without help. India still has far too few rehab specialists for this scale. Rest and painkillers are often the only options on offer. Surgery, when it happens, is rarely followed by proper recovery.</p><p>Physiotherapy changes the outcome. Guided movement reduces pain, rebuilds strength, and can delay or avoid surgery. After a stroke, a fracture, a delivery, or years at a desk, the right routine restores independence. When trusted physio tools reach clinics and homes beyond a handful of cities, recovery stops being a privilege.</p><p>VA Healthcare exists to put clinic-grade physiotherapy products into India’s medical sales network — so more people can move again, work again, and age with dignity.</p>",
        "help_heading": "How physiotherapy helps",
        "caption": "Impact figures drawn from COPCORD India community studies (~16% MSK pain; ~200 million people) and national surveys of adults 45+ (over half report musculoskeletal disorders).",
